What happened is a previous game of yours crashed, and Nethack is
asking if it's okay to get rid of the old temp files from that game in
order to start a new one.

As a game of Nethack continues, the program creates a number of
temporary files in a working directory, including one per dungeon level
in the current game.  Further, if Nethack is compiled with checkpoint
support enabled, some extra info is saved somewhere, so that the
recover tool can be used to restore the game from the last level
change.  This is not the same as a saved game, although recover can use
them to create a save game file.

If you had access to the alt.org server, you could run recover in order
to get your old game back and continue.  Basically, all you can do at
this point is either email the site maintainer to try to get him to run
recover for you, or, if you don't care about it, you can choose to
reset the game playground in order to start over.

I, and at least one other person, have had similar problems there in
the past, and emailing the site maintainer didn't do any good.
However, previously others have managed to get crashed games restored.
In any case, eventually it seems that the temporary files will get
deleted automatically.

